# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# The committed fixture trees are compared byte for byte against what the
# generators re-encode, so the bytes on disk have to be the bytes in the blob.
# `text=auto` above normalizes on commit but still writes CRLF into the working
# tree wherever core.autocrlf is true, which is every Windows clone. The three
# byte-exact assertions in conformance (TestEncodeSkeletonIsIdempotent,
# TestExpandSkeletonIsTheInverseOfEncode, and TestLiveBaselineIsCanonical's
# re-render check) then fail on all 55 live fixtures and on the live baseline,
# for a reason that has nothing to do with the SDK. These are data, not source:
# nothing diffs them line by line, so marking them -text is the narrower fix than
# turning normalization off for the whole repository.
conformance/testdata/** -text
conformance/live-divergences.json -text
conformance/known-divergences.json -text
